# ============================================================
#  functions/.env.example — Phase 19, Workstream 3
# ============================================================
#
# Copy this file to functions/.env and fill in REAL (but non-secret) values
# before deploying functions. Phase 18, Workstream 3 decided that ordinary,
# non-secret runtime config lives here, in plain functions/.env — separately
# from the five real secrets, which live ONLY in Google Secret Manager (see
# functions/.secret.local.example for local emulator access to those).
#
# functions/.env is gitignored via `Agrimore-main/.gitignore:49`'s `.env`
# pattern (confirmed with `git check-ignore -v functions/.env`) — NOT via
# functions/.gitignore's `*.local` pattern, which is a different mechanism
# that only covers functions/.secret.local. Do not assume one covers the
# other for a differently-named file.
#
# NEVER put a real value in this .example file. NEVER commit functions/.env
# itself.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRAP F — READ THIS BEFORE RESTORING ANY BACKUP INTO functions/.env
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The owner's keystore/secrets backup archive contains a file at
# AGRIMORE_PLAYSTORE_AND_SECRET_KEYS_BACKUP/05_FIREBASE_FUNCTIONS_AND_ROOT/
# functions.env that declares BOTH RAZORPAY_KEY_ID and RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET.
# Restoring that file verbatim as functions/.env would put a Secret Manager
# -bound secret back into a plain env file and silently undo Phase 18's
# hardening. RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET (or any of the other four Secret Manager
# secret names — RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET, TWOFACTOR_API_KEY,
# OTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY) must NEVER appear as a key in this
# file. Only the keys below belong in functions/.env.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Returned directly to the client in createRazorpayOrder's response
# (payment.ts:33 / payment.ts:78) — Razorpay key IDs are public by design,
# required by the checkout SDK. Putting this in Secret Manager would cost
# money/IAM overhead for zero security benefit. See the Phase 18,
# Workstream 3 decision comment directly above the read site in payment.ts.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=your_razorpay_key_id_here

# NOTE: there is deliberately NO TWOFACTOR_SMS_TEMPLATE setting here.
# 2Factor's custom-OTP endpoint (the one smsProvider.ts uses, where WE supply
# the code) is documented as exactly
#   POST https://2factor.in/API/V1/{key}/SMS/{phone}/{otp}
# with NO template parameter. template_name applies only to the AUTOGEN form
# and to the newer JSON endpoint POST /API/V1/OTP/SEND. Appending it to the
# custom-OTP path was tried 2026-08-30, had no effect, and was reverted — see
# the OPEN ISSUE comment above sendSmsOtp() in smsProvider.ts before
# re-attempting it.

# The from-address on every email sendEmailOTP sends (emailProvider.ts:38)
# — appears in the email header itself, nothing to protect. Must be on a
# domain verified in the Resend dashboard. See the Phase 18, Workstream 3
# decision comment directly above the read site in emailProvider.ts.
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@your-verified-domain.example

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 22 — phone OTP channel availability
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-secret: a plain on/off switch, not a credential. Read by
# sendPhoneOTP.ts, independently of PHONE_OTP_ENABLED (which answers "is a
# provider configured at all"). This one answers "of the channels that
# provider offers, which ones may we actually use".
#
# Set to "false" (or leave unset) while this account has no usable DLT
# registration — see the OPEN ISSUE comment above sendSmsOtp() in
# smsProvider.ts. While disabled, EVERY phone OTP request is delivered by
# voice call regardless of what the client asks for, and the stricter
# MAX_VOICE_SENDS_PER_DAY cap in sendPhoneOTP.ts does NOT apply — voice
# requests are governed by the combined MAX_SENDS_PER_DAY (10) instead, so
# voice-as-primary doesn't lock a real user out of the app.
#
# Only the exact string "true" enables SMS. Anything else — unset, "",
# "false", "1", "yes" — is treated as disabled (fail closed on typos).
#
# THE ONE-LINE CHANGE FOR WHEN DLT REGISTRATION COMPLETES: set this to
# "true". No other code change is needed — the SMS-first channel
# resolution, the stricter voice cap, and the honest response `channel`
# field all revert to their originally-designed behaviour automatically.
PHONE_OTP_SMS_ENABLED=false
